Looking at the four failures, two (sp0536, sp0600) are duplicate-row fan-out — already tried twice in r1 with zero gain. The other two are a different pattern: **projection width**. sp0755 returns only `Name` when gold returns all 19 columns of the joined tables; sp0894's invented-column anti-join returns 0 rows and the repair can't recover because it never sees the real columns of the relationship table. Both stem from the model guessing column scope instead of grounding on schema facts.

I'll target projection width + grounded schema feedback rather than re-attempting dedup. One edit to solve.py: (a) strengthen entity-projection guidance toward `SELECT *` over joins for whole-entity questions, (b) feed actual referenced-table columns into repair feedback so invented columns get corrected.

